{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"PLAN-REVIEW STATUS (3 cycles, still BLOCK — deep AC5 spec gap). Cycle 1: transient LLMUnavailableError. Cycle 2 (real): 2 G6 blocks — AC5 mechanism unspecified, AC10 equivalence contradicted its own deletion blind-spot. Remediated both (chose merge-onto-prior-snapshot; scoped AC10 to observable classes). Cycle 3 surfaced 4 DEEPER code-grounded blocks that invalidate that mechanism:\n1) AC1 invalidates tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_jira_datacenter_backend_port.py::test_dc_backend_is_deliberately_not_incremental (asserts DC is NOT incremental) — AC7 must enumerate its disposition (delete or invert to assert DC now satisfies SupportsIncremental).\n2) AC5 merge base is UNSOUND as written: the persisted prior snapshot (.tickets-tracker/.bridge_state/prev_snapshot.json, written by reconcile.py _write_prev_snapshot_key_set ~L557) is KEY-MEMBERSHIP ONLY with empty bodies ({jira_key: {}}), not full content — so upsert-by-key cannot reconstruct a complete curr_snapshot. fetcher.py:751-754 writes a full snapshot to bridge_state/snapshots/<pass>.json but it is DIAGNOSTIC/ephemeral and never loaded into the diff path.\n3) The prior snapshot is available in reconcile.py _load_snapshots (ctx.prev_snapshot, ~L263-299), NOT in fetcher.py _build_snapshot (which takes no prior-snapshot arg). Relocate AC5 there or thread prior state in explicitly.\n4) AC5 must mandate a FULL-SCAN FALLBACK (not incremental merge) whenever the merge base is empty/missing/corrupt (fresh run: prev_snapshot=={}; or _handle_corrupt_snapshot path), with a test pinning that an incremental fetch onto an empty base never reaches the differ as a standalone/partial snapshot. AC2 currently gates fallback on isinstance (capability presence), not on merge-base availability.\nNEXT: rewrite AC5 to either (a) SCOPE persisting a full-content prior curr_snapshot as the merge base + carry-forward unchanged keys + full-scan fallback on empty/corrupt base, OR (b) confine incremental to a field-update path that NEVER feeds absence/edge detection (which keeps requiring a full scan). Then fix AC7 test disposition, re-run review-plan. reconcile.py snapshot model confirmed by direct read."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786126736510744001,"uuid":"4d430817-ccf6-4a18-baeb-1fcd3d2ee802"}